72	    /// usage emits one Usage followed by Finish on `message_stop`). A
73	    /// terminal event (`Finish` or an `Err`) is emitted at most once per
74	    /// stream, and a later `message_delta`'s `Usage` is suppressed once one
75	    /// has been emitted. Content deltas are deliberately *not* guarded: a
76	    /// malformed stream that keeps sending `content_block_delta` after
77	    /// `message_stop` would still yield them. A clean end-of-stream flush of
78	    /// a buffered stop reason with no terminal event yet is handled
